  "第三名死者的住宅没有尸体，只有两封彼此指控的遗书和一道无法由房间灯位形成的第二影子。拉普拉斯听见墙内残留的呼救，特蕾莎在她开口前说出死者从未登记过的名字。她们没有同行，也没有接受我们的指挥，却仍完成了暮钟馆训练出的旧分工。白粉笔不是凶手签名，而是在要求一个外部见证者把矛盾压成唯一事实。": "The third victim's home holds no body, only two wills accusing each other and a second shadow that the room's lamps cannot make. Laplace hears the cry for help left in the wall, and Theresa speaks, before she opens her mouth, a name the victim never registered. They did not travel together, nor take our orders, yet they still completed the old division the Duskbell Hall trained into them. The white chalk is no killer's signature, but a demand that an outside witness press the contradiction into a single fact.",
