  "04:03 — 调谐台在两条同样清晰的声纹之间拒绝给出真伪指示。": "04:03 — Between two equally clear sound-prints the tuning bench refuses to indicate true or false.",
  "05:12 — 特蕾莎第一次承认，她害怕的不是记错，而是两段都没有记错。": "05:12 — Theresa admits for the first time that what she fears is not misremembering, but that neither memory is wrong.",
  "艾达把播放钥匙分开藏匿，是为了阻止暮钟馆只公开一只蜡筒。拉普拉斯的录音里，她找到出口并不断请求特蕾莎不要敲钟；特蕾莎的录音里，她已经无法完整说话，请求对方阻止自己出去。两段背景声纹属于同一个时刻，均无拼接。回声调谐台只能帮助我们对齐频段，不能替任何人判定唯一版本。暮钟真正制造的是两段都能独立成立的现实。": "Ada hid the playback keys apart to stop the Duskbell Hall from releasing only one cylinder. In Laplace's recording she finds the exit and keeps begging Theresa not to strike the bell; in Theresa's, she can no longer speak whole and begs the other to stop her from going out. Both background sound-prints belong to the same moment, neither spliced. The tuning bench can only help us align the frequencies, not decide a single version for anyone. What the Duskbell truly makes are two realities that each stand on their own.",
  "当两份录音共享同一秒钟的所有背景细节时，哪一项证据还能允许我们把其中一份降格为谎言？": "When both recordings share every background detail of the same second, what evidence could still let us demote one of them to a lie?",
  "被登记册剪掉的一分钟": "The Minute the Register Cut Away",
  "缺失的一分钟不是空白，而是暮钟让第三见证者进入两段现实的门。": "The missing minute is no blank, but the door by which the Duskbell lets a third witness enter both realities.",
  "计时署保存每一秒的责任人，唯独把 23:43 之后的一分钟归档为从未发生。": "The timekeeping office keeps a person responsible for every second, filing only the minute after 23:43 as never having happened.",
