  "01:44 — 日志后半出现第二种笔迹，内容却早于书写者出生。": "01:44 — A second hand appears in the log's later half, its content older than the writer's birth.",
  "02:59 — 不成对手套分别保留拉普拉斯与特蕾莎的旧训练磨痕。": "02:59 — The unpaired gloves keep, each on its own, Laplace's and Theresa's old training wear.",
  "04:10 — 最终见证表只允许勾选一个真实版本。": "04:10 — The final witness form allows only one true version to be ticked.",
  "05:15 — 费利克斯承认暮钟不在乎勾哪一格，只在乎有人愿意删掉另一格。": "05:15 — Felix admits the Duskbell does not care which box is ticked, only that someone is willing to delete the other.",
  "市政登记册把 23:43 之后的一分钟整齐剪掉，所有受暮钟影响的怀表也留下同样缺口。第二种笔迹不是附身，而是历代第三见证者预写的行政语气。最终表格要求未参与旧案的人选择唯一版本；一旦签名，另一个人便会被现实当作污染残余删除，钟后聆听者则从被删除的矛盾中取得入口。费利克斯不关心谁正确，他只需要我们相信真相必须唯一。": "The municipal register cuts the minute after 23:43 away cleanly, and every watch touched by the Duskbell keeps the same gap. The second hand is no possession, but the administrative tone that generations of third witnesses wrote in advance. The final form asks a person who took no part in the old case to choose one version; once signed, the other is deleted by reality as contaminating residue, and the listener behind the bell takes its entrance from the deleted contradiction. Felix does not care who is right; he needs only that we believe the truth must be single.",
  "如果暮钟能自行辨认真相，仪式为什么非要等待一个外部人填完空白裁决格？": "If the Duskbell can tell the truth by itself, why must the ritual wait for an outsider to fill in the blank verdict box?",
  "第十三声钟": "The Thirteenth Bell",
  "巨钟等待一份唯一报告，两名旧猎手却第一次交换了被训练好的位置。": "The great bell waits for a single report, yet the two old hunters swap, for the first time, the positions they were trained into.",
  "城市愿意容纳十二声报时；第十三声只在有人准备删去另一段人生时出现。": "The city will hold twelve tolls of the hour; the thirteenth appears only when someone is ready to delete another life.",
  "证据应当公开、封存，还是拒绝替两段真实记忆指定唯一主人？": "Should the evidence be made public, sealed, or should we refuse to name a single owner for two true memories?",
